---
title: Network Managers
order: 7
description: connmanctl, nmcli, nmtui
tags: [connman, connmanctl, networkmanager, nmcli, nmtui]
---

ConnMan and NetworkManager are the two main network management daemons.
ConnMan is lighter weight and common on Artix/OpenRC setups. NetworkManager
is more feature-rich and integrates with KDE Plasma.

@code bash
# ---- ConnMan: connmanctl ----

# OpenRC service
rc-service connmand start
rc-update add connmand default

# connmanctl interactive mode
connmanctl
> technologies                            # list available technologies
> enable wifi                             # enable wifi
> scan wifi                               # scan for networks
> services                                # list available services
> agent on                                # enable authentication agent
> connect wifi_xxxx_managed_psk           # connect (will prompt for passphrase)
> disconnect wifi_xxxx_managed_psk        # disconnect
> quit

# connmanctl non-interactive
connmanctl technologies
connmanctl enable wifi
connmanctl scan wifi
connmanctl services
connmanctl connect wifi_xxxx_managed_psk
connmanctl disconnect wifi_xxxx_managed_psk

@code bash
# connmanctl service details
connmanctl services wifi_xxxx_managed_psk   # full details of a service

# static IP configuration
connmanctl config wifi_xxxx_managed_psk --ipv4 manual 192.168.1.100 255.255.255.0 192.168.1.1
connmanctl config wifi_xxxx_managed_psk --nameservers 8.8.8.8 1.1.1.1

# back to DHCP
connmanctl config wifi_xxxx_managed_psk --ipv4 dhcp

# tethering
connmanctl tether wifi on "HotspotName" "passphrase"
connmanctl tether wifi off

@text
ConnMan stores profiles in /var/lib/connman/. Each service gets a
directory with a settings file. You can edit these directly:

@code bash
# /var/lib/connman/wifi_xxxx_managed_psk/settings
[wifi_xxxx_managed_psk]
Name=MyNetwork
Passphrase=secret
AutoConnect=true
Favorite=true

@text
NetworkManager is the alternative, especially useful with KDE Plasma where
it provides the system tray network applet.

@code bash
# ---- NetworkManager: nmcli ----

# OpenRC service
rc-service NetworkManager start
rc-update add NetworkManager default

# general status
nmcli general status                      # overall status
nmcli device status                       # device list and state
nmcli connection show                     # saved connections
nmcli connection show --active            # active connections only

@code bash
# wifi
nmcli device wifi list                    # scan and list networks
nmcli device wifi connect "MyNetwork" password "secret"       # connect
nmcli device wifi connect "MyNetwork" password "secret" ifname wlan0  # specific device
nmcli device wifi connect "HiddenSSID" password "secret" hidden yes   # hidden network
nmcli connection up "MyNetwork"           # activate saved connection
nmcli connection down "MyNetwork"         # deactivate
nmcli device disconnect wlan0             # disconnect device

@code bash
# connection management
nmcli connection add type ethernet con-name "Work" ifname eth0 \
  ipv4.method manual ipv4.addresses "192.168.1.100/24" \
  ipv4.gateway "192.168.1.1" ipv4.dns "8.8.8.8 1.1.1.1"

nmcli connection modify "Work" ipv4.dns "8.8.8.8"
nmcli connection modify "Work" ipv4.method auto    # back to DHCP
nmcli connection delete "Work"
nmcli connection reload                   # reload from disk

# VPN
nmcli connection import type openvpn file client.ovpn
nmcli connection up client

@code bash
# nmcli networking and radio control
nmcli networking on                       # enable networking
nmcli networking off                      # disable networking
nmcli radio wifi on                       # enable wifi radio
nmcli radio wifi off                      # disable wifi radio

# hotspot
nmcli device wifi hotspot ifname wlan0 ssid "MyHotspot" password "secret"

# DNS
nmcli device show eth0 | grep DNS        # show DNS servers

@code bash
# ---- nmtui: text user interface ----

nmtui                                     # interactive TUI
nmtui-connect                             # connect to a network
nmtui-edit                                # edit connections
nmtui-hostname                            # set hostname

@text
Do not run ConnMan and NetworkManager simultaneously. They will conflict
over interface management. Choose one and disable the other.

KDE Plasma integration: NetworkManager provides the plasma-nm applet in
the system tray. If using ConnMan, the tray applet is connman-qt or
cmst (ConnMan System Tray).

@code bash
# check which is running
rc-status | grep -E 'connman|Network'

# switch from ConnMan to NetworkManager
rc-service connmand stop
rc-update del connmand default
rc-service NetworkManager start
rc-update add NetworkManager default
